        "also_known_as": [],
        "biography": "Gordon Jennings,\u00a0A.S.C.\u00a0(1896 \u2013 January 11, 1953) was an American\u00a0special effects\u00a0artist. He received seven\u00a0Academy Awards\u00a0(mainly for\u00a0Best Special Effects) and was nominated for eight more in the same category. After starting in 1919 in Hollywood as\u00a0a camera assistant,\u00a0he worked from 1932 until 1953 on the visual and special effects of more than 180 films. His older brother was cinematographer Devereaux Jennings (1884-1952), who filmed, for instance,\u00a0Buster Keaton's monumental\u00a0The General\u00a0in 1926.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Gordon Jennings, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.",
